# oracle: pair_style uf3 2 on bcc Nb (the 2-body block of the example's Nb.uf3: 2B Nb Nb, non-uniform knots), 4x4x4 bcc cell (128 atoms, a = 3.3005), 50 NVE steps at 300 K (the example in.uf3.Nb without its 3-body term)
# measured (engine vs native, max rel over |value| >= 1e-6; atoms scaled by max(1,|value|)): thermo pe/temp/press max rel 5.9e-15; per-atom xu,yu,zu,vx,vy,vz,fx,fy,fz max 6.8e-14
# native: b332f28 (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, package ML-UF3 installed); the potential is Nb.uf3 of the example (examples/PACKAGES/uf3)
# oracle-potentials: Nb.uf3
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           metal
boundary        p p p
lattice         bcc 3.3005
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 92.906
pair_style      uf3 2
pair_coeff      * * Nb.uf3 Nb
thermo_style    custom step temp pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          10
timestep        0.5e-3
neighbor        1.0 bin
neigh_modify    once no every 1 delay 0 check yes
velocity        all create 300.0 2367804
fix             1 all nve
run             50
